{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Why.</b> They fast and say to HaShem, 'Why did we fast and You did not see?' — as though He does not see and does not know. And the meaning is: You do not save us. And the answer: 'Yes, on the day of your fast everyone finds his desire' — whoever has a quarrel with another person:" "<b>And all your toil.</b> Money, like 'your toil in the house of a stranger' (Proverbs 5:10). And it is close to the derivation of 'toil' (Genesis 3:17), like 'the labor of your hands' (Psalms 128:2):" "<b>You exact.</b> The nun [in תנגושו] is like the nun [in כהנדוף] 'like the driving of smoke' (Psalms 68:3). And it lacks 'master,' as if it said 'master of toils.' And like it: 'a woman who fears YHWH' (Proverbs 31:30), and many like this."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:08.608099590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}